// diagnostics-project-an-unsaved-declaration-still-falls-back.test.maxon — a `didChange` that ADDS A `type`
// DECLARATION the corpus never swept must leave the project view, and the publish that follows is EMPTY
// and arrives on a LIVE session.
//
// ⭐⭐⭐ **THIS IS NOT A CORNER CASE. IT IS THE BOUNDARY THE WHOLE PROJECT-VIEW FEATURE STANDS ON, AND
// ANYONE ABOUT TO WIDEN THE GUARD SHOULD READ IT FIRST.** The project view parses the LIVE buffer's tokens
// against the signature index the corpus swept FROM DISK. That is sound only while the buffer cannot have
// changed anything the index holds — and the index holds far more than declarations. Which methods carry
// the hidden descriptor and how many parameters they take is decided by scanning BODIES, so an edit that
// leaves every declaration alone can still change the ABI a caller's parse emits against; `spawn X.y()`
// typed into a body mints whole new TYPES through `discoverWholeProgramTokenFacts` →
// `synthesizeServiceCompanions`. ⇒ **"this edit cannot have moved anything" is a claim about at least six
// classes of body fact, and most of them nobody can currently rule out.** The guard the buffer must be
// token-for-token the disk's is what covers all of them at once.
//
// ⛔⛔⛔ **A REGRESSION HERE READS AS THE SESSION DYING, NOT AS A FAILED ASSERTION.** Parsing a buffer
// against a signature index that does not hold the type the buffer declares is not a wrong answer — it is
// a PANIC, verbatim:
//
//     panic at Parser.maxon:78284: enclosingLayout: `type ProjectUnsavedWidget` is being parsed right now,
//     but the declaration sweep never recorded it - `recordScannedType` and `parseTypeDeclaration` disagree
//     about what opens a type declaration
//
// A panic ends the PROCESS, so no second publish ever arrives: the framed stream breaks and the probe
// reports `the framed stream broke — …` rather than a diagnostic count. ⇒ **read a red here as "the server
// died", and go looking for a panic rather than for a wrong count.**
//
// ⛔⛔ **AND IT IS ONE OF ROUGHLY TWENTY INDEX-DISAGREEMENT PANICS REACHABLE FROM `parseFile`, OF WHICH
// ABOUT A DOZEN CANNOT CURRENTLY BE RULED OUT AT ALL.** `Parser.maxon:55639` is the one the minted service
// companions reach. ⇒ **the narrow guard is not conservatism — it is the only defensible line**: a guard
// that admits a class of edit is a claim about every one of those twenty, and nobody can make a dozen of
// them today.
//
// ⭐ An edit that moves the token stream off the disk's falls back to the per-buffer compile, so this
// assertion is a pin on the road already taken and not a request for a new one.
//
// The staged project is a REAL one and so is the edited text — both build, so a red here cannot mean the
// fixture is broken. ⚠ The edited buffer is SELF-CONTAINED on purpose: it names nothing the sibling file
// exports, because the fallback compiles the buffer against `stdlib/` and `runtime/` alone and any sibling
// name in it would redden this case for a reason that has nothing to do with the declaration. The session,
// the staging and the assertions are `diagnostics-project-probe.test.maxon`'s.

let ProjectUnsavedEditDirName = "diagnostics-project-unsaved-edit"
let ProjectUnsavedEditDeclaringFileName = "slot.maxon"
let ProjectUnsavedEditBufferFileName = "main.maxon"
let ProjectUnsavedEditDeclaringSource = "export typealias ProjectUnsavedEditSlot = int(0 to u64.max)\n"
let ProjectUnsavedEditSavedSource = "function main() returns ExitCode\n\tlet n = 1 as ProjectUnsavedEditSlot\n\treturn n as ExitCode\nend 'main'\n"
let ProjectUnsavedEditTypedSource = "type ProjectUnsavedEditWidget\n\texport let width as ExitCode\n\n\tstatic function create(width ExitCode) returns ProjectUnsavedEditWidget\n\t\treturn Self\{width: width\}\n\tend 'create'\nend 'ProjectUnsavedEditWidget'\n\nfunction main() returns ExitCode\n\tlet widget = ProjectUnsavedEditWidget.create(0)\n\treturn widget.width\nend 'main'\n"

test 'a didChange that declares a type the index never swept still falls back'
	let root = stagedProjectDiagnosticsRoot(ProjectUnsavedEditDirName)
	writeCorpusFile(root, fileName: ProjectUnsavedEditDeclaringFileName, content: ProjectUnsavedEditDeclaringSource)
	writeCorpusFile(root, fileName: ProjectUnsavedEditBufferFileName, content: ProjectUnsavedEditSavedSource)

	let probes = probeProjectDiagnosticsAcrossAnEdit(root, fileName: ProjectUnsavedEditBufferFileName, content: ProjectUnsavedEditSavedSource, editedContent: ProjectUnsavedEditTypedSource)

	discardOutsideCheckoutDir(root)

	expectNoProjectDiagnostics(projectDiagnosticsPublish(probes, index: ProjectDiagnosticsAtOpen), note: "the buffer opened holding exactly the disk's bytes, and `ProjectUnsavedEditSlot` is `export typealias`ed by the sibling file, so the project view is taken and nothing is published. This publish is the CONTROL: a diagnostic here is the project view failing at `didOpen`, before any edit, and says nothing about the edit below.")

	expectNoProjectDiagnostics(projectDiagnosticsPublish(probes, index: ProjectDiagnosticsAfterTheEdit), note: "⛔ READ THIS RED AS A DEAD SERVER, NOT AS A WRONG COUNT. The `didChange` declares `type ProjectUnsavedEditWidget` and uses it, and the corpus's signature index has never swept that name. An edit that adds a declaration MUST leave the project view: parsing this buffer against that index PANICS in `enclosingLayout`, `recordScannedType` and `parseTypeDeclaration` disagreeing about what opens a type declaration — and a panic ends the process, so what arrives is a broken frame stream rather than a diagnostic. The edited text is self-contained and `maxon build` compiles it, so the only correct publish is an empty one.")
end 'a didChange that declares a type the index never swept still falls back'
